  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Kings",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 1,
    "summary": "Abishag cherishes David in his extreme age—Adonijah aspires to be king—Bathsheba and Nathan advise David of Adonijah’s plotting—David names Solomon as king, and he is anointed by Zadok—Adonijah’s cause fails.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Now king David was old and stricken in years; and they covered him with clothes, but he gat no heat.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 26
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:1",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore his servants said unto him, Let there be sought for my lord the king a young virgin: and let her stand before the king, and let her cherish him, and let her lie in thy bosom, that my lord the king may get heat.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 142,
            "end": 149,
            "text": "IE wait upon."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:2",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "So they sought for a fair damsel throughout all the coasts of Israel, and found Abishag a Shunammite, and brought her to the king.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 52,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "OR borders."
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 87,
            "text": "1 Kgs. 2:17."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
