        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "But Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and Nathan the prophet, and Shimei, and Rei, and the mighty men which belonged to David, were not with Adonijah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 125,
            "end": 133
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:8",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And Adonijah slew sheep and oxen and fat cattle by the stone of Zoheleth, which is by En-rogel, and called all his brethren the king’s sons, and all the men of Judah the king’s servants:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:9",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "But Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah, and the mighty men, and Solomon his brother, he called not.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:10",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "Wherefore Nathan spake unto Bath-sheba the mother of Solomon, saying, Hast thou not heard that Adonijah the son of Haggith doth reign, and David our lord knoweth it not?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 162,
            "end": 164
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:11",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Now therefore come, let me, I pray thee, give thee counsel, that thou mayest save thine own life, and the life of thy son Solomon.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:12",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "Go and get thee in unto king David, and say unto him, Didst not thou, my lord, O king, swear unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne? why then doth Adonijah reign?",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 139,
            "text": "1 Chr. 22:9."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "1 Chr. 22:9.",
            "prettyString": "1 Chronicles 22:9",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "1chronicles",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 22,
                    "end": 22,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 9,
                        "end": 9
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:13",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "Behold, while thou yet talkest there with the king, I also will come in after thee, and confirm thy words.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:14",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "And Bath-sheba went in unto the king into the chamber: and the king was very old; and Abishag the Shunammite ministered unto the king.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:15",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "And Bath-sheba bowed, and did obeisance unto the king. And the king said, What wouldest thou?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:16",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "And she said unto him, My lord, thou swarest by the Lord thy God unto thine handmaid, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 44,
            "text": "2 Sam. 12:24 (15–25)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:17",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And now, behold, Adonijah reigneth; and now, my lord the king, thou knowest it not:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 78
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:18",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And he hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the sons of the king, and Abiathar the priest, and Joab the captain of the host: but Solomon thy servant hath he not called.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:19",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And thou, my lord, O king, the eyes of all Israel are upon thee, that thou shouldest tell them who shall sit on the throne of my lord the king after him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:20",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "Otherwise it shall come to pass, when my lord the king shall sleep with his fathers, that I and my son Solomon shall be counted offenders.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:21",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "And, lo, while she yet talked with the king, Nathan the prophet also came in.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:22",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "And they told the king, saying, Behold Nathan the prophet. And when he was come in before the king, he bowed himself before the king with his face to the ground.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:23",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And Nathan said, My lord, O king, hast thou said, Adonijah shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:24",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "For he is gone down this day, and hath slain oxen and fat cattle and sheep in abundance, and hath called all the king’s sons, and the captains of the host, and Abiathar the priest; and, behold, they eat and drink before him, and say, God save king Adonijah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 234,
            "end": 256,
            "text": "HEB May King Adonijah live (long)!"
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:25",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "But me, even me thy servant, and Zadok the priest, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada, and thy servant Solomon, hath he not called.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 12
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:26",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "Is this thing done by my lord the king, and thou hast not shewed it unto thy servant, who should sit on the throne of my lord the king after him?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 67
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:27",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "Then king David answered and said, Call me Bath-sheba. And she came into the king’s presence, and stood before the king.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:28",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And the king sware, and said, As the Lord liveth, that hath redeemed my soul out of all distress,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 32
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:29",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "Even as I sware unto thee by the Lord God of Israel, saying, Assuredly Solomon thy son shall reign after me, and he shall sit upon my throne in my stead; even so will I certainly do this day.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:30",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "Then Bath-sheba bowed with her face to the earth, and did reverence to the king, and said, Let my lord king David live for ever.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 30
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:31",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 31
      },
      {
        "text": "And king David said, Call me Zadok the priest, and Nathan the prophet, and Benaiah the son of Jehoiada. And they came before the king.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 32,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:32",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 32
      },
      {
        "text": "The king also said unto them, Take with you the servants of your lord, and cause Solomon my son to ride upon mine own mule, and bring him down to Gihon:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 146,
            "end": 151,
            "text": "2 Chr. 32:30."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 33,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "2 Chr. 32:30.",
            "prettyString": "2 Chronicles 32:30",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "2chronicles",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 32,
                    "end": 32,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 30,
                        "end": 30
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Kings 1:33",
        "book": "Kings",
        "chapter": 1,
        "verse": 33
      },
      {
        "text": "And let Zadok the priest and Nathan the prophet anoint him there king over Israel: and blow ye with the trumpet, and say, God save king Solomon.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "1 Sam. 10:1; 1 Kgs. 2:15; 1 Chr. 29:22."
          },
          {
